{
  "info": {
    "name": "gateway-2 (open-rlb/nestjs-amqp) — setup & test playlist",
    "description": "Ordered, runnable playlist for the gateway-2 example, using a REAL Keycloak login.\n\nWHAT IT DOES (top-to-bottom, via the Collection Runner):\n0. **Logs in** to Keycloak (direct access / password grant) as {{kcUsername}} -> stores {{token}} and decodes the access_token `sub` into {{userId}}.\n1. Creates ACL **actions** (gateway-access, admin-access).\n2. Creates ACL **roles** (user, admin) that bundle those actions.\n3. Creates the **user association** (grant): {{userId}} (the Keycloak sub) -> [user].\n4. Verifies the **protected** route: 200 when granted, 401 without a token, then revoke -> 403 -> re-grant -> 200.\n5. Drives **gateway-admin**: DB routes (create/list/export), auth-providers, metrics.\n6. Tests the **DB-loaded** route after a restart.\n\nBEFORE RUNNING:\n- The gateway-2 app must be up (`nest start gateway-2` or F5 -> 'Debug gateway-2') with Mongo/Redis/RabbitMQ reachable.\n- The Keycloak client {{kcClientId}} must have 'Direct Access Grants' enabled (public client; no secret).\n- Run on a FRESH Mongo DB the first time: the revoke -> 403 step assumes a single grant per user.\n\nThe gateway verifies the Keycloak access_token via the `gateway-jwks` provider (issuer + JWKS, RS256), maps `sub` -> X-GTW-AUTH-USERID and calls AclService.canUserDo('rlb-acl','gateway-access', sub) in-process (RAM + Redis L2 cache, then Mongo).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000" },
    { "key": "kcTokenUrl", "value": "https://login.riolabs.net/realms/riolabs-dev/protocol/openid-connect/token" },
    { "key": "kcClientId", "value": "chattoo" },
    { "key": "kcUsername", "value": "riolo.giuseppe@gmail.com" },
    { "key": "kcPassword", "value": "!1Ciao" },
    { "key": "token", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "ebd36ac4-5633-4434-b402-ab3b8b9e0a7b" },
    { "key": "lastPathId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "lastAuthId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "lastActionId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 · Auth & health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST Login (Keycloak password grant)",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "pm.test('login ok (200)', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200); });",
              "var j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.expect(j.access_token, 'access_token in response').to.be.a('string');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', j.access_token);",
              "// decode the JWT payload (base64url) to capture the Keycloak subject as {{userId}}",
              "function decodeJwt(t){",
              "  var seg = t.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g,'+').replace(/_/g,'/');",
              "  var json = (typeof atob !== 'undefined') ? atob(seg) : Buffer.from(seg, 'base64').toString('binary');",
              "  return JSON.parse(json);",
              "}",
              "var payload = decodeJwt(j.access_token);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', payload.sub);",
              "pm.test('captured Keycloak sub -> {{userId}}', function () { pm.expect(payload.sub).to.be.a('string'); });",
              "console.log('Logged in as', payload.preferred_username || payload.email, '(sub=' + payload.sub + ')');"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                { "key": "grant_type", "value": "password" },
                { "key": "client_id", "value": "{{kcClientId}}" },
                { "key": "username", "value": "{{kcUsername}}" },
                { "key": "password", "value": "{{kcPassword}}" },
                { "key": "scope", "value": "openid profile" }
              ]
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{kcTokenUrl}}", "host": ["{{kcTokenUrl}}"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "pm.test('gateway is up (200)', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200); });"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["health"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /protected  (403 — logged in but not yet granted)",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "// Valid Keycloak token passes auth, but with no ACL grant the role check fails.",
              "pm.test('Forbidden (403) before the grant exists (fresh DB)', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([403, 200]); });",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) { console.log('NOTE: already 200 — a grant for this user persists from a previous run.'); }"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{token}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/protected", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["protected"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
